  "details": "It would be great if there is transparent variant of Toon Standard shader for fallback and in-SDK shader.\n\nThere are many usage of transparent in avatars like:\n\n - facial expressions like blushing, heart eyes, shocked face\n\n - sun glasses\n\n - Manga iconography\n\n - fake shadow of hair on the face\n\n - Clothings with thin fabric \n\n - Hairs, especially bangs transparent/translucent eyes and eyebrows\n\n - VRoid Avatars\n\nIt would be great if we can express such situations with fallback shaders, and if there are such variants, we can make avatars with exactly same looking as fallback and non-fallback shaders.\n\nIn addition it would be perfect if we can change render queue for transparent materials (including fallbacked ones).\n\nImages are provided by ku10by. Thanks a lot.\n\nImage 1: Manga iconography and bangs transparent/translucent eyes and eyebrows (Maya)\n\nImage 2&3: facial expressions, heart eyes, and transparent/translucent eyes and eyebrows (Moe)\n\nImage 4: fake shadow (Sephira)\n\nImage 5: vinyl / transparent skirt (Sapphy)\n\nRelated Canny: Request for toon transparent fallback shaders from era of toonlit https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-the-transparent-toon-shader-to-the-fallback-system",
